===Funeral===
A Scildist funeral typically comprises two burials. During the initial burial of the body in a burial chamber, the body is left to decompose for about a year to obtain a bare skeleton. During the secondary burial, the deceased's family gathers the bones, which are then piled up in bulk before being stacked in [[wikipedia:ossuary|ossuaries]]. Once an ossuary is full, the bones are transferred to a common grave during a second funeral service to which the entire local community is invited. 

Scildist ossuaries are often decorated with the bones of deceased people, making them museums of the dead. Due to lack of space, larger cities usually have [[wikipedia:catacombs|catacombs]], which are underground ossuaries. Catacombs, although most notable as underground passageways and ossuaries, also house many decorations and sculptures dedicated to the dead. The [[Catacombs of Zhifol]], beneath the [[Palace of Zhifol]], are particularly famous for being the resting place of all the members of the [[House of Zhifol]], the ruling royal family of [[Qym]]. Other famous Scildist catacombs include the [[Catacombs of Zhol]], by far the largest, and also the [[Catacombs of Teurek]] for its unique decorative ornaments. 

During the [[Festival of the Dead]], Scildists perform an evening communal procession to the local ossuary with candles and various skull-related iconography, from makeup, masks or baked goods shaped like skulls. This festival honors all the deceased and a person's ancestors, making it one of the most important in Scildism. Specific regional varieties regarding this festival are found throughout Basis, but it is generally considered a continuation of funeral practices and a way to respect the deceased long after their death.

